1
00:00:03,545 --> 00:00:04,672
Joey?

2
00:00:04,713 --> 00:00:06,173
Are you in there?

3
00:00:06,214 --> 00:00:07,215
God, that's Rachel!

4
00:00:07,257 --> 00:00:09,009
Joey, you have to talk to her.

5
00:00:09,050 --> 00:00:10,093
Oh, no, I can't, I can't.

6
00:00:10,135 --> 00:00:11,261
Not after the other night.

7
00:00:11,303 --> 00:00:12,513
It's too weird, okay?

8
00:00:12,554 --> 00:00:14,014
Don't tell her I'm here.

9
00:00:16,391 --> 00:00:17,852
Don't eat that!

10
00:00:18,978 --> 00:00:21,104
Hi.
Hey, Rachel.

11
00:00:21,146 --> 00:00:22,397
Is Joey here?

12
00:00:22,439 --> 00:00:23,941
I don't see him.
Do you see him?

13
00:00:23,983 --> 00:00:25,233
I don't see him.

14
00:00:25,275 --> 00:00:26,276
Hey, maybe he's
in the sugar bowl.

15
00:00:26,318 --> 00:00:27,820
Joey? No.

16
00:00:27,862 --> 00:00:29,196
( both laugh )

17
00:00:29,237 --> 00:00:31,657
Well, at least you make
each other laugh.

18
00:00:32,992 --> 00:00:34,117
What's up?

19
00:00:34,159 --> 00:00:35,703
Well, I haven't seen him

20
00:00:35,744 --> 00:00:38,789
since the night that he told me
how he, you know...

21
00:00:38,831 --> 00:00:41,750
I don't know, I think
he's avoiding me.

22
00:00:41,792 --> 00:00:43,002
Why is that bagel
on the floor?

23
00:00:45,629 --> 00:00:46,797
We were playing
a game.

24
00:00:46,839 --> 00:00:48,757
Ew, was Chandler naked?

25
00:00:50,759 --> 00:00:54,179
Sort of like a ring-toss
kind of situation?

26
00:00:54,221 --> 00:00:55,639
Sure.

27
00:00:55,681 --> 00:00:57,975
What? No... no!

28
00:00:58,017 --> 00:01:00,644
All right, well, listen,
if you see Joey

29
00:01:00,686 --> 00:01:05,649
will you just tell him
that, uh... I miss him.

30
00:01:07,275 --> 00:01:08,819
( door closes )

31
00:01:10,612 --> 00:01:12,322
Okay, did you hear that?

32
00:01:12,364 --> 00:01:15,075
Yeah, that naked bagel game?

33
00:01:17,077 --> 00:01:18,245
Dude, I don't know.

34
00:01:18,286 --> 00:01:20,080
That's a pretty small hole.

35
00:01:22,917 --> 00:01:24,877
Honey, you've got
to talk to her.

36
00:01:24,919 --> 00:01:26,085
I can't.

37
00:01:26,127 --> 00:01:27,421
You guys don't know
what it's like

38
00:01:27,462 --> 00:01:28,756
to put yourself out there
like that

39
00:01:28,797 --> 00:01:29,965
and then just get shot down.

40
00:01:30,007 --> 00:01:31,717
I don't know
what that's like?

41
00:01:31,759 --> 00:01:33,010
Up until I was 25

42
00:01:33,052 --> 00:01:35,303
I thought the only
response to "I love you"

43
00:01:35,345 --> 00:01:36,847
was, "Oh, crap."

44
00:01:36,889 --> 00:01:38,390
And hello--

45
00:01:38,432 --> 00:01:39,474
no rejection?

46
00:01:39,516 --> 00:01:42,143
I got shot down
at fat camp.

47
00:01:43,144 --> 00:01:45,856
Boy, kids are mean
when they're hungry.

48
00:01:47,983 --> 00:01:50,193
All right, so what do I do?

49
00:01:50,235 --> 00:01:51,653
This is Rachel.

50
00:01:51,695 --> 00:01:53,572
What are you going to do--
never talk to her again?

51
00:01:53,614 --> 00:01:55,532
I know it's weird,
it's awkward

52
00:01:55,574 --> 00:01:56,951
but you got to
at least try.

53
00:01:56,992 --> 00:01:59,703
Yeah, okay.

54
00:02:01,830 --> 00:02:03,832
Whoa! Almost forgot
this was on your...

55
00:02:03,874 --> 00:02:05,876
We didn't play it!

56
00:02:12,424 --> 00:02:17,679
♪ So no one told you
life was gonna be this way ♪

57
00:02:17,721 --> 00:02:19,932
♪ Your job's a joke,
you're broke ♪

58
00:02:19,974 --> 00:02:22,059
♪ Your love life's D.O.A. ♪

59
00:02:22,101 --> 00:02:26,897
♪ It's like you're always
stuck in second gear ♪

60
00:02:26,939 --> 00:02:29,190
♪ When it hasn't been
your day, your week ♪

61
00:02:29,232 --> 00:02:32,444
♪ Your month,
or even your year ♪

62
00:02:32,486 --> 00:02:35,739
♪ But I'll be there for you ♪

63
00:02:35,781 --> 00:02:41,745
♪ 'Cause you're there
for me, too. ♪

64
00:02:46,416 --> 00:02:48,167
Okay, so when you're done
with your tea

65
00:02:48,209 --> 00:02:50,545
I'll look at the leaves
and tell you your fortune.

66
00:02:50,587 --> 00:02:52,047
I didn't know
you read tea leaves.

67
00:02:52,089 --> 00:02:53,799
Oh, yeah. I've
done it for years.

68
00:02:53,841 --> 00:02:56,217
I actually stopped
because I was so accurate.

69
00:02:56,259 --> 00:02:57,594
You know and... you know

70
00:02:57,636 --> 00:02:59,429
one of the great joys
of life

71
00:02:59,471 --> 00:03:03,266
is its wondrous
unpredictability, you know.

72
00:03:03,308 --> 00:03:06,185
And also tea tends
to give me the trots.

73
00:03:06,227 --> 00:03:08,605
Okay, I'm done.
Read mine.

74
00:03:08,647 --> 00:03:10,774
Okay... Ooh.

75
00:03:10,816 --> 00:03:12,442
I see a ladder...

76
00:03:12,484 --> 00:03:15,612
which can mean
either a promotion

77
00:03:15,654 --> 00:03:17,531
or a violent death.

78
00:03:21,076 --> 00:03:22,410
I'm a head chef.

79
00:03:22,452 --> 00:03:24,287
I can't get promoted.

80
00:03:24,329 --> 00:03:26,373
Mm-hmm, Mm-hmm...
who's next?

81
00:03:27,708 --> 00:03:28,834
Okay, I'm done.

82
00:03:28,876 --> 00:03:29,835
Do mine.

83
00:03:29,877 --> 00:03:31,086
Okay.

84
00:03:31,128 --> 00:03:33,047
Um... oh, okay.

85
00:03:33,088 --> 00:03:35,007
I see a circle.

86
00:03:35,049 --> 00:03:38,385
Oh, which can either mean
you're having a baby

87
00:03:38,426 --> 00:03:41,889
or you're going to make
a scientific discovery.

88
00:03:41,930 --> 00:03:45,851
Well, I have been spending
a lot of time in the lab.

89
00:03:46,894 --> 00:03:48,187
What does yours say, Pheebs?

90
00:03:48,227 --> 00:03:51,065
Well, all right.

91
00:03:51,106 --> 00:03:53,232
Wow... yay!

92
00:03:53,274 --> 00:03:55,861
Oh, I'm going to meet a guy!

93
00:03:55,903 --> 00:03:58,072
And really soon!

94
00:03:58,113 --> 00:04:00,281
And he's going to be
the man of my dreams.

95
00:04:00,323 --> 00:04:03,911
Probably not the guy
I had a dream about last night.

96
00:04:07,372 --> 00:04:10,209
Hey, has anyone seen my shirt?

97
00:04:10,250 --> 00:04:14,421
It's button-down,
like a faded salmon color.

98
00:04:14,462 --> 00:04:16,924
You mean
your pink shirt?

99
00:04:16,965 --> 00:04:19,259
Faded salmon color.

100
00:04:19,300 --> 00:04:22,554
No, I haven't seen
your pink shirt.

101
00:04:22,596 --> 00:04:23,597
Great, great.

102
00:04:23,638 --> 00:04:25,348
I must have left it at Mona's.

103
00:04:25,390 --> 00:04:26,850
I knew it.

104
00:04:26,892 --> 00:04:28,852
I'm sure you can get another one
at Ann Taylor's.

105
00:04:31,396 --> 00:04:33,065
That's my favorite shirt, okay?

106
00:04:33,107 --> 00:04:34,108
I love that shirt.

107
00:04:34,149 --> 00:04:36,317
Just ask Mona to give it back.

108
00:04:36,359 --> 00:04:37,569
I don't know.

109
00:04:37,611 --> 00:04:39,279
I mean, I guess I could.

110
00:04:39,320 --> 00:04:41,698
It's just, we didn't really
end things on such good terms.

111
00:04:41,740 --> 00:04:43,283
And if I went over there

112
00:04:43,324 --> 00:04:45,119
I'd be ignoring the one thing
she asked me to do

113
00:04:45,160 --> 00:04:49,372
when we broke up:
jump up my own ass and die.

114
00:04:52,793 --> 00:04:54,461
Oh, wait a second,
you guys.

115
00:04:54,502 --> 00:04:56,255
For the last couple
of weeks

116
00:04:56,296 --> 00:04:58,924
I've been seeing that guy
everywhere I go.

117
00:04:58,966 --> 00:05:01,593
We take the same bus,
we go to the same bookstores

118
00:05:01,635 --> 00:05:02,761
same dry cleaners...

119
00:05:02,803 --> 00:05:04,429
May be he's the tea guy.

120
00:05:07,766 --> 00:05:09,226
Pheebs,
did you see that?

121
00:05:09,268 --> 00:05:11,645
He totally checked you out
and he is so cute!

122
00:05:16,316 --> 00:05:18,318
Mine is a picture
of the Village People.

123
00:05:18,359 --> 00:05:19,486
What does that mean?

124
00:05:23,949 --> 00:05:25,659
Hi.

125
00:05:25,700 --> 00:05:27,494
Hey.

126
00:05:39,047 --> 00:05:40,966
Hi.

127
00:05:41,008 --> 00:05:42,759
Hi.

128
00:05:50,017 --> 00:05:52,477
Tea gives Phoebe
the trots.

129
00:06:00,235 --> 00:06:01,320
So, I thought Joey and I

130
00:06:01,360 --> 00:06:02,696
would be okay
once we hung out

131
00:06:02,737 --> 00:06:04,198
but it's like we
don't even know

132
00:06:04,239 --> 00:06:05,824
how to be with each
other anymore.

133
00:06:05,866 --> 00:06:08,118
I know it's tough now,
but things'll get better.

134
00:06:08,160 --> 00:06:09,828
How do you know that?

135
00:06:09,870 --> 00:06:11,872
What if it just
gets worse and
worse and worse

136
00:06:11,913 --> 00:06:13,372
to the point where

137
00:06:13,414 --> 00:06:15,334
we can't even be
in the same room
with each other?

138
00:06:15,374 --> 00:06:17,711
I'm not great at the advice.

139
00:06:17,752 --> 00:06:21,256
Can I interest you
in a sarcastic comment?

140
00:06:23,008 --> 00:06:25,177
Some cheese?

141
00:06:27,012 --> 00:06:29,097
Honey...

142
00:06:29,139 --> 00:06:32,767
why is the Bruce Springsteen CD
in the Cat Stevens case?

143
00:06:32,809 --> 00:06:35,145
Let's just say if I can't find
the right CD case

144
00:06:35,187 --> 00:06:36,813
I just put it
in the nearest one.

145
00:06:36,855 --> 00:06:39,358
Okay, well, where is
the Cat Stevens CD?

146
00:06:39,398 --> 00:06:40,734
In the James Taylor case.

147
00:06:40,775 --> 00:06:42,485
Where's the James Taylor CD?

148
00:06:42,527 --> 00:06:44,487
Honey, I'm going to save you
some time.

149
00:06:44,529 --> 00:06:46,823
200 CDs, not one of them
in the right case.

150
00:06:46,865 --> 00:06:49,993
Okay, no need to panic.

151
00:06:50,035 --> 00:06:53,038
Deep breaths everyone.

152
00:06:53,080 --> 00:06:55,332
Okay, um, we're just going
to have to spend some time

153
00:06:55,374 --> 00:06:56,833
and put the CDs
in the right cases.

154
00:06:56,875 --> 00:06:59,002
Then we should come up
with some kind of order.

155
00:06:59,044 --> 00:07:01,296
You know, like alphabetically
or by genre.

156
00:07:01,338 --> 00:07:02,714
Mmm, I don't know.
I think we're going

157
00:07:02,756 --> 00:07:04,132
to have to talk this through.

158
00:07:04,174 --> 00:07:06,927
Oh, my God, you guys
have such problems.

159
00:07:06,968 --> 00:07:09,096
I feel so terrible for you.

160
00:07:11,431 --> 00:07:13,267
Okay, I-I'm sorry.

161
00:07:13,308 --> 00:07:14,601
Look, you and Joey

162
00:07:14,642 --> 00:07:16,519
you're both focusing
on this uncomfortable thing.

163
00:07:16,561 --> 00:07:18,605
What you need to do
is change the subject.

164
00:07:18,646 --> 00:07:20,107
Next time you see him

165
00:07:20,148 --> 00:07:21,900
try to get him talking
about something else.

166
00:07:21,942 --> 00:07:23,693
Oh, yeah, that makes sense.

167
00:07:23,735 --> 00:07:25,320
Yeah, like, I don't know
maybe you have

168
00:07:25,362 --> 00:07:27,155
a work problem
that you need his advice on.

169
00:07:27,197 --> 00:07:28,156
Ooh, I could do that.
Good.

170
00:07:28,198 --> 00:07:29,741
I could do that.

171
00:07:29,783 --> 00:07:32,702
Honey, the Miami Vice
soundtrack? Really?

172
00:07:32,744 --> 00:07:35,038
They were just giving those away
at the store.

173
00:07:36,248 --> 00:07:38,457
In exchange for money.

174
00:07:40,961 --> 00:07:42,712
Hey.

175
00:07:42,754 --> 00:07:45,048
Hi.

176
00:07:47,592 --> 00:07:50,595
I really don't know
what to tell you, Rach.

177
00:07:50,637 --> 00:07:51,763
I really don't.

178
00:07:51,805 --> 00:07:54,266
I mean, maybe Joey
could help you out

179
00:07:54,308 --> 00:07:56,226
with your big work problem.

180
00:07:56,268 --> 00:07:57,352
What?

181
00:07:57,394 --> 00:07:58,686
Yeah, Joey, she's...

182
00:07:58,728 --> 00:08:01,522
Rachel's got this really
big work problem.

183
00:08:01,564 --> 00:08:03,150
It is a head-scratcher.

184
00:08:04,901 --> 00:08:06,069
Wow, you know what?

185
00:08:06,111 --> 00:08:07,695
If we're going to make dinner

186
00:08:07,737 --> 00:08:09,614
we're going to have to leave.
Yeah.

187
00:08:12,742 --> 00:08:16,246
So, you, uh,
have a big work problem?

188
00:08:16,288 --> 00:08:19,791
Yeah, it's, um...

189
00:08:19,833 --> 00:08:21,960
Yeah... it's, uh...

190
00:08:24,587 --> 00:08:27,007
It's noth...
you know, it's nothing.

191
00:08:27,048 --> 00:08:29,176
Oh, okay.

192
00:08:32,553 --> 00:08:35,390
So, uh, I think
I'm going to take off.

193
00:08:35,432 --> 00:08:37,225
No, wait, Joey, no, wait.

194
00:08:37,267 --> 00:08:39,186
It is. It's something.

195
00:08:39,227 --> 00:08:40,937
It's-it's, um...

196
00:08:40,979 --> 00:08:42,356
It's my boss.

197
00:08:42,397 --> 00:08:43,440
Yeah?

198
00:08:43,482 --> 00:08:45,566
Yeah, and, um...

199
00:08:45,608 --> 00:08:48,278
and my baby.

200
00:08:49,737 --> 00:08:50,905
Yeah?

201
00:08:50,947 --> 00:08:54,326
My boss wants to buy my baby.

202
00:08:56,453 --> 00:08:58,205
What?

203
00:08:58,246 --> 00:09:00,332
Oh, my... oh, my God.

204
00:09:00,374 --> 00:09:03,751
I know, I told you
it's a really big problem.

205
00:09:03,793 --> 00:09:06,296
What... he wants
to buy your baby?

206
00:09:06,338 --> 00:09:07,672
Can you believe that?

207
00:09:07,714 --> 00:09:08,840
That's crazy.

208
00:09:08,882 --> 00:09:10,633
That's what I told him.

209
00:09:10,675 --> 00:09:11,718
Okay, how did this
even happen?

210
00:09:11,759 --> 00:09:13,636
Well, I'll tell you...

211
00:09:16,973 --> 00:09:19,059
See, my-my boss and, uh...

212
00:09:19,100 --> 00:09:22,103
and his wife,
they can't have children

213
00:09:22,145 --> 00:09:26,316
so, um, and then when we were
at the Christmas party

214
00:09:26,358 --> 00:09:28,568
and he got drunk
and he said to me

215
00:09:28,609 --> 00:09:31,279
"Rachel,
I want to buy your baby."

216
00:09:31,321 --> 00:09:34,366
Man. When you said
it was a problem

217
00:09:34,408 --> 00:09:36,034
about your boss
and the baby

218
00:09:36,076 --> 00:09:38,537
I figured it was something
about maternity leave.

219
00:09:38,578 --> 00:09:40,914
Oh... yeah...

220
00:09:51,216 --> 00:09:54,928
Yeah, that would have been
a much simpler problem.

221
00:10:02,310 --> 00:10:03,728
Oh, hello.
Oh.

222
00:10:03,770 --> 00:10:04,729
It's you.

223
00:10:04,771 --> 00:10:06,398
I see you everywhere.

224
00:10:06,440 --> 00:10:07,399
Mm-hmm.

225
00:10:07,441 --> 00:10:08,775
I'm Jim. Jim Nelson.

226
00:10:08,816 --> 00:10:11,236
Oh, Jim-Jim Nelson,
I'm Phoebe-Phoebe Buffay.

227
00:10:11,278 --> 00:10:12,695
We certainly
have been seeing

228
00:10:12,737 --> 00:10:14,655
a lot of each other lately.

229
00:10:14,697 --> 00:10:15,907
We have.

230
00:10:15,949 --> 00:10:17,158
Maybe we'll be
seeing each other

231
00:10:17,200 --> 00:10:18,410
at dinner tomorrow night.

232
00:10:18,452 --> 00:10:19,453
Say around 8:00?

233
00:10:19,494 --> 00:10:22,289
Well, maybe we will.

234
00:10:23,706 --> 00:10:24,749
Oh!

235
00:10:31,005 --> 00:10:32,632
Mona?

236
00:10:44,102 --> 00:10:46,020
( falsetto yelp )

237
00:10:56,656 --> 00:11:00,910
Okay, if I were a salmon shirt,
where would I be?

238
00:11:00,952 --> 00:11:02,621
( keys rattling )

239
00:11:08,001 --> 00:11:12,297
I am so sorry I spilled wine
all over your shirt.

240
00:11:12,339 --> 00:11:13,590
Oh, it's okay.

241
00:11:13,632 --> 00:11:14,924
No, it's still wet.
You know what?

242
00:11:14,966 --> 00:11:16,259
Let me get it out
before it sets.

243
00:11:16,301 --> 00:11:18,136
Oh, I have something
you could wear.

244
00:11:21,473 --> 00:11:22,474
Here.

245
00:11:22,516 --> 00:11:24,476
Oh, uh...

246
00:11:24,518 --> 00:11:26,978
I don't know if I want
to wear a woman's shirt.

247
00:11:29,397 --> 00:11:30,898
No, no, that's a man's shirt.

248
00:11:30,940 --> 00:11:31,941
Awfully pink.

249
00:11:37,280 --> 00:11:38,490
Oh, my God, honey

250
00:11:38,532 --> 00:11:40,283
we are so meant
to be together.

251
00:11:40,325 --> 00:11:42,701
Look, we both have copies
of the Annie soundtrack.

252
00:11:42,743 --> 00:11:44,954
Honey, both yours.

253
00:11:46,540 --> 00:11:49,708
Hey, great advice
on that Joey thing.

254
00:11:49,750 --> 00:11:51,169
Yeah? The work problem?

255
00:11:51,211 --> 00:11:52,711
Oh, it was perfect.

256
00:11:52,753 --> 00:11:54,755
I mean, it really felt
like he was my friend again.

257
00:11:54,797 --> 00:11:56,132
What problem did you
tell him you have?

258
00:11:56,174 --> 00:11:58,801
Oh, that's-that's not important.

259
00:11:58,843 --> 00:12:00,928
The point is, I really...

260
00:12:00,970 --> 00:12:04,057
I think everything's
going to be okay.

261
00:12:04,098 --> 00:12:06,934
May I help you?

262
00:12:06,976 --> 00:12:11,356
You think you can just
buy my friend's baby?

263
00:12:18,405 --> 00:12:19,573
Isn't it funny

264
00:12:19,614 --> 00:12:21,616
how we kept running
